<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-04--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-04: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.35";
    dc:description "Comparative compilations of brain size, neuron number, and learning scores exist as scattered published tables and can be tested for saltations versus grades on those proxies. No single public matrix covers cognition across the claim's full range of organisms, and competing proxies answer differently. The result can pressure a strong binary reading and cannot settle cognitive capacity as such.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: On one pre-registered cognitive or neural trait, test whether sister lineages differ by jumps that are large relative to within-lineage variation and short relative to individual lifespan; a continuum holds if changes are graded on that trait.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Have not been shown' is a claim about the literature as well as about the organisms.", "A graded proxy can hide a qualitative change in a capacity the proxy does not measure.", "Neuron counts, brain size, and learning scores are different operationalizations and need not agree.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.35"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-04--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2022-tame-04 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
